<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spanish–Portuguese War (1776–1777)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1776–1777</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Spanish–Portuguese War of 1776–1777 was fought over the borderlands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a> and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>. A large Spanish expedition under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-cevallos">Pedro de Cevallos</a> took the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santa-catarina">Santa Catarina</a> and the colony of Sacramento in 1777. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-treaty-of-san-ildefonso">First Treaty of San Ildefonso</a> of 1777 gave Sacramento and the Banda Oriental to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and returned Santa Catarina to Portugal.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spanish-portuguese-war-1776-1777.jpg" alt="Spanish–Portuguese War (1776–1777)" width="320" height="459" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carlos Julião · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pinto_Bandeira_de_Minas_Geraes_contra_os_hespanhoes_(crop).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
